      "writtenOn": "2024-09-20T09:08:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would it be possible to have a `DAWN_ASSERT` that `usage` is a subset of a `kTextureUsageRequiringViews` defined around [1]? Likewise an assert in `ValidateCanUseAs(TextureBase)` that we don\u0027t have any of the view usages. This would make sure that when we add more `ValidateCanUseAs` calls in the future we do it on the correct object (view or parent texture). (I\u0027m not actually sure if this invariant that view and non-view usages are disjoint isn\u0027t already broken in some way by the WebGPU spec).",
      "revId": "cd7d35f0da0138220c3ad2379d8c99e61eb964be",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
